package pages

import "strconv"

import "github.com/atknatk/tappa/web/templates/components"

// MANUAL RECORD ENTRY (M6-08) — the one screen in this panel that WRITES an
// attendance record, and the only place the product ever puts an hour on somebody's
// payroll without a physical touch behind it.
//
// 🔴 IT RENDERS PanelShell, NOT PanelShellWithScript. This screen loads no script:
// two steps, two ordinary form posts, no fragment. That keeps the panel's widened
// Content-Security-Policy on exactly ONE url, which is the cardinality
// TestPanelScreens_ScriptsAndPolicyAgreeAndReachNoThirdParty pins — and it is why the
// confirmation is a SERVER step rather than a browser dialog: a dialog is not
// something a server can require, which is the argument the deactivation flow already
// makes.
//
// 🔴 §4.3 — TWO STEPS, AND THE SECOND ONE EXISTS BECAUSE THE WRITE IS PERMANENT.
// `transactions` takes no UPDATE and no DELETE. §4.3's own remedy — a correction is a
// NEW row — was measured against the report engine and only works in half the
// directions (internal/domain/manual's CorrectionsOnlyShorten): an appended record can
// make a shift shorter and never longer. So the warning below is not decoration, and
// the sentence it carries is a measurement rather than a caution.
//
// 🔴 THE WRITE BUTTON CANNOT BE RENDERED BEFORE THE WARNING, AND WHAT HOLDS THAT IS
// THE `if v.Confirming` BRANCH BELOW — measured, after this paragraph claimed
// otherwise. It said the VIEW held it ("RecordAction is empty on the first step, so
// there is no address for the button to point at"), and a mutation refuted it: setting
// RecordAction on the first step changes nothing, because the first step never renders
// it. The empty field is a consequence, not a barrier.
//
// So the barrier is one `if`, and it is asserted as one:
// TestManualForm_NeverRendersTheWriteFormNoMatterWhatTheViewCarries drives this
// template with the write address AND a confirmation token set and Confirming false,
// and requires the write form to be absent. What stands behind it if it ever failed is
// the SERVER: the write route verifies a confirmation bound to this exact record, so a
// form rendered early would still be refused.
//
// skill tappa-brand governs the surface: the kitchen docket is the record motif, every
// instant and every identifier is IBM Plex Mono, the status-to-colour mapping is the
// unchanging one, and nothing is carried by colour alone — the deactivation warning, the
// permanence warning and every refusal say their own words.
//
// THE REDESIGN (M12-33, boards Manual · T-Manual · M-Manual; screen file people.md §4).
// The shell carries the heading: the trail back to the person, the eyebrow, the title,
// and the two steps at the title's right (manualSteps). The tab stays The Pass. The body
// is the docket with the form or the summary in it and, beside it from the desk width and
// under it below that, what the record will look like once it is written and what this
// screen does to the table. There is no third step: a written record answers with a
// redirect to the record itself on The Pass (manualRecordReturn), so the steps say
// "Fill in" and "Check" and nothing more.
templ AdminManualEntry(v ManualEntryView) {
	@PanelActions(manualSteps(v.Confirming)) {
		@PanelShell(v.PanelChrome) {
			if v.Problem != "" {
				// A REFUSAL IS AN ALERT: something the manager asked for was not done, and
				// the label the notice opens with says exactly that before the heading says
				// why.
				@components.PanelNotice(components.ToneAlert, manualProblemHeading(v.Problem)) {
					switch v.Problem {
						case "direction":
							<p>A record is either a check-in or a checkout, and nothing was chosen. Nothing was written.</p>
						case "venue":
							<p>{ v.Name } has no home venue, so the record needs the venue the shift was worked at. Nothing was written.</p>
						case "when":
							// THE CLOCK IS THE BUSINESS'S, NOT A VENUE'S: manualInstant reads the
							// wall clock in the tenant's zone, and the zone line under the fields
							// says the same words.
							<p>We could not read that date and time, so nothing was written. Both fields are needed, in this business&#39;s own clock.</p>
						case "future":
							<p>That moment has not happened yet. A record is a statement about work already done, so nothing was written.</p>
						case "too-old":
							// THE BOUND IS DESCRIBED RATHER THAN QUOTED. The number lives in
							// internal/domain/manual, and a copy of it here is a second
							// representation that goes stale silently — the class this repository
							// has paid for repeatedly.
							<p>That date is further back than this screen accepts, so nothing was written. Check the year first: it is the field that goes wrong most often.</p>
						case "confirm-required":
							<p>Nothing was written. Entering a record needs the confirmation screen first, and this one either was not used or was left open too long.</p>
							<p class="mt-1">Fill the form again; the button appears under the summary.</p>
						case "confirm-stale":
							<p>Nothing was written. This browser is in the middle of confirming a different record, so the button you pressed no longer matches.</p>
							<p class="mt-1">Start this one again and confirm from its own summary — one confirmation at a time.</p>
						case "unavailable":
							<p>Nothing was written. We could not prepare the confirmation step, so the record was not offered for confirmation either. Try again in a moment.</p>
						default:
							<p>Nothing was written.</p>
					}
				}
			}
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-6 desk:flex-row desk:flex-wrap desk:items-start">
				<section class="docket flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-4 px-4 pb-[22px] pt-[18px] md:gap-[18px] md:px-6 md:pb-[26px] md:pt-[22px] desk:flex-[999_1_520px] desk:gap-5 desk:px-7 desk:pb-[30px] desk:pt-[26px]" aria-label="Enter a record by hand">
					<div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
						<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-1">
							<p class="lbl">Attendance record</p>
							<h2 class="break-words font-display text-[22px] font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink md:text-2xl desk:text-[26px]">
								{ v.Name }
							</h2>
							<p class="text-xs text-ink/70 md:text-[13px]">
								if v.Venue != "" {
									{ v.Venue }
								} else if v.NeedsVenue {
									// K-14: somebody the integration manages, placed by no venue. The
									// record is filed at the venue chosen below.
									no home venue
								} else {
									venue not recorded
								}
								if v.Department != "" {
									· { v.Department }
								}
							</p>
						</div>
						// A RECORD STARTS FROM A PERSON, so changing the person is going back to
						// the roster, the one place a manager picks somebody.
						<a class="inline-flex min-h-11 flex-none items-center font-display text-sm font-bold text-tappa-green underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href={ templ.URL(v.PeopleHref) }>Someone else?</a>
					</div>
					if v.Deactivated {
						// 🔴 SAID, NOT REFUSED. Somebody's last shift is often typed after they
						// have left, and refusing it would create an unpayable shift with no way
						// back — deactivation is one-way and this table takes no UPDATE. What the
						// screen owes the manager is the fact, before the button.
						<div class="font-display">
							@components.PanelNotice(components.ToneWarn, "This person has been deactivated") {
								<p>
									Their own taps are refused from now on. A record you type here is still
									written and still counts, which is what makes a final shift payable —
									so make sure this is the person you mean.
								</p>
							}
						</div>
					}
					if v.Confirming {
						@manualConfirmStep(v)
					} else {
						@manualFormStep(v)
					}
				</section>
				<aside aria-label="How it will look" class={ manualAsideClass(v.Confirming) }>
					if v.Confirming {
						// THE RECORD AS THE DAY'S LEDGER WILL DRAW IT: the ledger's own docket
						// component over the view the handler built the ledger's way
						// (manualPreview). Its stamp is APPROVED because a manual record is
						// written ok, and the manager's tally marks it; the stamps are verdicts
						// only, so there is no stamp for "manual".
						<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3.5">
							<p class="lbl">How it will look on The Pass</p>
							@components.TransactionDocket(v.Preview)
						</div>
					}
					<div class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2">
						<p class="font-display text-sm text-ink">This adds a new record. Nothing existing is changed.</p>
						// WHAT "SHOWN APART" MEANS IS THE CODE'S: every manual record carries the
						// manager's tally on The Pass, and The Roll and the CSV count the
						// check-ins a manager typed.
						<p class="field-help">
							Manual records are counted in hours. On The Pass each one carries the mark
							that a manager entered it, and The Roll and the CSV show apart the
							check-ins a manager typed.
						</p>
					</div>
				</aside>
			</div>
		}
	}
}

// manualSteps is the step progress at the title's right: "1 Fill in" and "2 Check", the
// whole of this flow (a written record is shown on The Pass, not on a third step). A
// static ordered list -- a step is reached by doing the one before it, so neither is a
// link -- with the current one marked for assistive technology and the finished one
// saying so in words as well as in its green.
//
// ON A PHONE the list is read but not drawn and a short line says which step this is:
// the boards print it in the phone's own words. From the tablet width the two pills are
// drawn. The list reserves a width the tablet's title row cannot also hold, so there it
// sits under the title as the tablet board draws it; from the desk width it sits at the
// title's right.
templ manualSteps(confirming bool) {
	<p aria-hidden="true" class="lbl md:hidden">
		if confirming {
			Step 2 of 2 · Check
		} else {
			Step 1 of 2 · Fill in
		}
	</p>
	<ol aria-label="Steps" class="sr-only md:not-sr-only md:flex md:min-w-[460px] md:flex-wrap md:gap-1.5 desk:min-w-0">
		<li
			class={ manualStepClass(1, confirming) }
			if !confirming {
				aria-current="step"
			}
		>
			1 Fill in
			if confirming {
				<span class="sr-only">, done</span>
			}
		</li>
		<li
			class={ manualStepClass(2, confirming) }
			if confirming {
				aria-current="step"
			}
		>
			2 Check
		</li>
	</ol>
}

// manualStepClass is one step's pill: the current step ink with paper text, a finished
// one a light green ground under ink text, a later one an outline. Every class is
// written here literally, so the stylesheet builder finds it.
func manualStepClass(n int, confirming bool) string {
	current := 1
	if confirming {
		current = 2
	}
	switch {
	case n == current:
		return "rounded-full border border-ink bg-ink px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-paper"
	case n < current:
		return "rounded-full border border-transparent bg-tappa-green/10 px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink"
	default:
		return "rounded-full border border-line px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-xs text-ink/70"
	}
}

// manualAsideClass lays out what sits beside the docket. On the second step it holds the
// preview and the notes: one column on a phone, the preview and the notes side by side on
// a tablet, one column beside the docket from the desk width. On the first step it holds
// the notes alone.
func manualAsideClass(confirming bool) string {
	if confirming {
		return "flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-3.5 md:grid md:grid-cols-[280px_minmax(0,1fr)] md:items-start md:gap-5 desk:flex desk:flex-[1_1_320px] desk:flex-col desk:gap-3.5"
	}
	return "flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-2 desk:flex-[1_1_320px]"
}

// manualTimeInvalid says whether the date and time are what a refusal is about, so the
// two fields carry the invalid state a screen reader hears and the frame a sighted
// manager sees.
func manualTimeInvalid(problem string) bool {
	return problem == "when" || problem == "future" || problem == "too-old"
}

// manualFormStep is what the manager fills in.
//
// THE FIELDS ARE THE WHOLE OF WHAT A CLIENT CONTRIBUTES: a person (carried unseen, and a
// narrowing value inside their own tenant), a direction from a closed vocabulary, a
// wall clock and a sentence. The venue and the department are NOT here — the write
// statement reads them off the employee row, so there is no field a manager could
// mis-file somebody through. The one exception is a person with NO home venue (K-14):
// the form then asks for the venue, and the statement reads it only for them.
templ manualFormStep(v ManualEntryView) {
	<form method="post" action={ templ.URL(components.Bound(ctx, v.Action)) } class="flex flex-col gap-4 font-display md:gap-[18px]">
		<input type="hidden" name="id" value={ v.EmployeeID }/>
		<fieldset class="flex flex-col">
			<legend class="lbl mb-2">What happened</legend>
			// REAL RADIOS, DRAWN AS CARDS. Each card is the label of its radio, so the
			// keyboard, a screen reader and a form post work with no script at all; the
			// radio itself is visually hidden and the card shows its checked and focused
			// states.
			<div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-2">
				for _, d := range v.Directions {
					<label class="manual-dircard">
						// THE ACCENT IS THE BRAND'S, NOT THE BROWSER'S (skill tappa-brand: stay
						// inside the palette). The radio is visually hidden today, but a browser
						// that draws it anyway (forced colours, a user stylesheet) must not paint
						// it the user agent's blue, the one colour this product does not use.
						<input
							class="peer sr-only accent-tappa-green"
							type="radio"
							name="direction"
							value={ d.Value }
							checked?={ v.Direction == d.Value }
						/>
						<span class="text-[15px] font-bold tracking-tight md:text-base">{ d.Label }</span>
						<span class="text-xs text-ink/70 md:text-[13px]">{ d.Sentence }</span>
					</label>
				}
			</div>
		</fieldset>
		if v.NeedsVenue {
			// 🔴 THE ONE PLACEMENT A MANAGER CHOOSES, AND ONLY HERE (K-14). Somebody with a
			// home venue is filed there by the statement itself and this control is not
			// rendered; somebody without one cannot be filed anywhere else. NO EMPTY
			// OPTION IS PRE-SELECTED AS A VENUE: the empty one says "choose", and
			// submitting it is refused with a sentence.
			<div class="field-stack">
				<label class="lbl" for="record-location">Venue</label>
				<select
					class="field-input"
					id="record-location"
					name="location"
					if v.Problem == "venue" && v.SiteID == "" {
						aria-invalid="true"
					}
				>
					<option value="" selected?={ v.LocationID == "" }>Choose the venue</option>
					for _, o := range v.Venues {
						<option value={ o.Value } selected?={ o.Value == v.LocationID }>{ o.Label }</option>
					}
				</select>
				<p class="field-help">
					{ v.Name } has no home venue, so the record is filed at the one you choose.
				</p>
			</div>
		}
		if len(v.PartnerVenues) > 0 {
			// M11 API-1c: a shift worked at another business of the group (ADR 0027 §9). The
			// record stays this business's; the other business sees that one of its venues was
			// named on it, marked as entered by this business, and counted in nothing.
			<div class="field-stack">
				<label class="lbl" for="record-site">At a partner business&#39;s venue (optional)</label>
				<select
					class="field-input"
					id="record-site"
					name="site"
					if v.Problem == "venue" && v.SiteID != "" {
						aria-invalid="true"
					}
				>
					<option value="" selected?={ v.SiteID == "" }>No — one of this business&#39;s venues</option>
					for _, o := range v.PartnerVenues {
						<option value={ o.Value } selected?={ o.Value == v.SiteID }>{ o.Label }</option>
					}
				</select>
				<p class="field-help">
					Choose one only if the shift was worked at another business of your group.
				</p>
			</div>
		}
		<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-3.5">
			<div class="field-stack">
				<label class="lbl" for="record-date">Date</label>
				<input
					class="field-input field-input--mono"
					id="record-date"
					type="date"
					name="date"
					value={ v.Date }
					autocomplete="off"
					if manualTimeInvalid(v.Problem) {
						aria-invalid="true"
					}
				/>
			</div>
			<div class="field-stack">
				<label class="lbl" for="record-time">Time</label>
				<input
					class="field-input field-input--mono"
					id="record-time"
					type="time"
					name="time"
					value={ v.Time }
					autocomplete="off"
					if manualTimeInvalid(v.Problem) {
						aria-invalid="true"
					}
				/>
			</div>
		</div>
		// 🔴 THE ZONE IS PRINTED BESIDE THE FIELDS, NOT ASSUMED. This is a person typing
		// a wall clock and a server deciding which instant that is; a screen that did not
		// say which clock would be inviting the one mistake it cannot take back.
		<p class="-mt-1.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-ink/85">
			Times are this business&#39;s own clock: <strong class="font-bold">{ v.Zone }</strong>
		</p>
		<div class="field-stack">
			<label class="lbl" for="record-note">Why (optional)</label>
			<textarea
				class="field-input field-input--mono py-2.5"
				id="record-note"
				name="note"
				rows="2"
				maxlength={ strconv.Itoa(v.MaxNote) }
				autocomplete="off"
			>{ v.Note }</textarea>
			<p class="field-help">
				It is shown on the record itself, next to the mark that says a manager typed
				it. &#34;Phone was flat&#34; or &#34;forgot to tap out&#34; is enough.
			</p>
		</div>
		// ON A PHONE THE TWO CONTROLS STAY IN REACH above the section bar while the form is
		// scrolled (the bar's class in input.css says how); from the tablet width they sit
		// at the end of the form.
		<div class="manual-actbar">
			<button class="btn btn--primary min-h-14 flex-1 rounded-[14px] px-[22px] md:min-h-[52px] desk:flex-none" type="submit">Review this record</button>
			<a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center px-2 font-display text-sm font-bold text-tappa-green underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href={ templ.URL(v.BackHref) }>Cancel</a>
		</div>
	</form>
}

// manualConfirmStep is the warning and the write.
//
// 🔴 IT PRINTS THE INSTANT IN BOTH CLOCKS. The local one, with its weekday, is what a
// manager checks against their memory of the shift; the ISO one is what the database
// will hold. Printing one alone is how somebody confirms a time they read in a zone
// nobody named — the same rule M6-07's CSV follows for the same reason.
//
// THE SUMMARY AND THE WARNING ARE INSIDE THE WRITE FORM, ahead of its button, so on a
// phone the button stays in reach while they are read and still comes after both in
// reading order. The form carries only hidden fields and the button: nothing on this step
// can be typed into, so what is posted is what the summary says.
templ manualConfirmStep(v ManualEntryView) {
	<form method="post" action={ templ.URL(components.Bound(ctx, v.RecordAction)) } class="flex flex-col gap-4 font-display">
		<div class="flex flex-col gap-1 rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ink/50 px-3.5 py-3 font-mono md:px-4 md:py-3.5">
			<p class="lbl">About to be recorded</p>
			<p class="text-sm font-bold text-ink md:text-[15px]">
				{ directionLabel(v) } — { v.Name } { directionSentence(v) }
			</p>
			<p class="text-[13px] text-ink md:text-sm">
				{ v.WhenLocal } <span class="text-ink/70">· { v.Zone }</span>
			</p>
			<p class="text-xs text-ink/70 md:text-[13px]">{ v.WhenUTC } UTC</p>
			if v.ChosenPartnerVenue != "" {
				<p class="text-[13px] text-ink md:text-sm">At { v.ChosenPartnerVenue } <span class="text-ink/70">· a partner business&#39;s venue</span></p>
			} else if v.ChosenVenue != "" {
				<p class="text-[13px] text-ink md:text-sm">At { v.ChosenVenue }</p>
			}
			if v.Backdated {
				<p class="text-xs text-ink/85 md:text-[13px]">
					This is a past moment. The record will say it happened then, and it will
					also carry the time you wrote it.
				</p>
			}
			if v.Note != "" {
				<p class="text-xs text-ink/85 md:text-[13px]">&#34;{ v.Note }&#34;</p>
			}
		</div>
		// THE PERMANENCE WARNING IS A NOTE, NOT A FAILURE NOTICE: the panel's alert notice
		// opens with "Not done", and nothing has failed here. It is drawn whole at every
		// width (ADR 0011) in the tomato frame the boards give it, the words in ink.
		<div role="note" class="flex flex-col gap-1.5 rounded-xl border border-tomato bg-tomato/5 px-3.5 py-3 text-sm leading-normal text-ink md:px-4 md:py-3.5">
			<p class="font-bold">This cannot be edited or removed afterwards</p>
			<p>
				Attendance records are permanent — nothing in Taptime can change one or take it
				back, because a record may be needed as evidence.
			</p>
			// 🔴 THE MEASURED HALF, AND IT IS THE PART A MANAGER WOULD NOT GUESS. Adding a
			// later record is the only correction there is, and it can only make a shift
			// SHORTER: the report pairs somebody's latest check-in with the earliest
			// checkout after it. A checkout typed too early cannot be undone by typing the
			// right one afterwards. docs/adr/0011 carries the table.
			<p>
				If this is wrong, adding another record later can shorten the shift but never
				lengthen it. Check the time before you press.
			</p>
			// 🔴 THE SECOND MEASURED HALF, AND IT IS SPECIFIC TO A CHECK-IN. Correcting one
			// leaves the earlier check-in open, and no later checkout can ever close it —
			// every attempt writes one more permanent record and one more wrong line on the
			// report (ADR 0011, measured over three attempts). A manager who is told only
			// about the money would keep pressing.
			if v.Direction == "in" {
				<p>
					And if you are fixing a check-in you already entered, the old one stays in
					&#34;needs action&#34; for good: nothing you enter afterwards can close it.
					Rather than correcting one, get this one right.
				</p>
			}
		</div>
		<input type="hidden" name="id" value={ v.EmployeeID }/>
		<input type="hidden" name="direction" value={ v.Direction }/>
		<input type="hidden" name="date" value={ v.Date }/>
		<input type="hidden" name="time" value={ v.Time }/>
		<input type="hidden" name="note" value={ v.Note }/>
		if v.LocationID != "" {
			<input type="hidden" name="location" value={ v.LocationID }/>
		}
		if v.SiteID != "" {
			<input type="hidden" name="site" value={ v.SiteID }/>
		}
		<input type="hidden" name={ v.ConfirmField } value={ v.ConfirmToken }/>
		<div class="manual-actbar">
			<button class="btn btn--primary min-h-14 flex-1 rounded-[14px] px-[22px] md:min-h-[52px] desk:flex-none" type="submit">Record it</button>
			<a class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center px-2 font-display text-sm font-bold text-tappa-green underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href={ templ.URL(v.BackHref) }>Cancel</a>
		</div>
		// WHERE THE BUTTON LEADS IS THE RECORD ITSELF (manualRecordReturn): The Pass on the
		// record's own day, narrowed to the records a manager entered.
		<p class="field-help">
			Recording takes you to The Pass on that day, showing the records a manager
			entered, this one among them.
		</p>
	</form>
}
